Third-party notice

This package declares one runtime dependency, installed from npm and **not**
vendored here:

  cos-nodejs-sdk-v5   (Tencent Cloud COS SDK, MIT licensed)

It is used only to sign the COS upload request for `ima_upload_file`. Two things
about that dependency are worth recording rather than leaving to `npm ls`:

  * It is deliberately loaded by **dynamic** import. The host half of a DSH
    plugin cannot use bare specifiers — DSH loads plugins through a symlink, and
    Node resolves a symlinked module's bare imports from the link's real path,
    which has no `node_modules` above it. See the module header of
    `lib/index.js` for the measured failure.
  * A hand-written COS signer was written first and **falsified** before this
    dependency was taken on: five derivation formulations all returned
    `SignatureDoesNotMatch` while the service echoed a canonical string
    byte-identical to the one being sent. `README.md` section 5 records the
    experiment.

No source from any third party is copied into this repository. The plugin
implements the Cordis plugin contract and the `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` parameter
schema contract against their published type declarations; it imports neither at
build time, so no DeepSeek Harness code is redistributed here.
